// The snowball process — why it is shaped the way it is.
// This externalizes the design rationale already argued in prose across the
// skills (using-snowball, brainstorming, writing-plans, executing-plans,
// finishing-a-development-branch, blast-radius, decision-logging,
// syncing-decisions-to-memory, recalling-project-context). It is a structural map
// of an argument made elsewhere, not the reasoning itself.

[Trustworthy-Agent-Dev]: Snowball makes agent-driven development trustworthy, reviewable, and resumable across sessions and harnesses.

// --- Forward spine: gates that carry an idea from intent to integrated code ---

[Skill-Gating]: Every session injects using-snowball, forcing a skill check before any response or action — even before clarifying questions.
[Design-Before-Code]: brainstorming is a hard gate: no implementation skill runs until a design is presented and the operator approves it.
[Plan-Before-Edit]: writing-plans turns an approved spec into a stepwise implementation plan before code is touched.
[Isolation]: using-git-worktrees gives feature work a workspace isolated from the current one.
[Test-First]: test-driven-development enforces red/green/refactor; systematic-debugging enforces root-cause-before-fix.
[Evidence-Before-Claim]: verification-before-completion requires running commands and showing output before any "done / passing / fixed" claim.
[Reviewed-Disposition]: requesting/receiving-code-review demand non-performative review; finishing-a-development-branch gates how work integrates (merge / PR / keep / discard).

<Forward-Spine>: A chain of gates moves work from intent to integrated, each refusing to advance until its precondition is met.
  (1) [Skill-Gating]
  (2) [Design-Before-Code]
  (3) [Plan-Before-Edit]
  (4) [Isolation]
  (5) [Test-First]
  (6) [Evidence-Before-Claim]
  (7) [Reviewed-Disposition]
  -----
  (8) Work cannot run ahead of its own justification: each stage blocks until the prior one is satisfied.

// --- Scope and risk: one envelope, four lifecycle moments ---

[Scope-At-Design]: blast-radius with the design preset right-sizes approach and plan choices using change-scope and failure-impact (report-only at design and plan handoff).
[Risk-Before-Action]: blast-radius with the pre-execution preset surfaces medium-or-higher action-risk and unknown-risk errors before a plan step runs, using the same approval phrase as decision-logging.
[Impact-At-Completion]: blast-radius with the completion preset summarizes the actual diff before merge/PR disposition (report-only; action-risk loud only for push/release-class next steps).

<Scope-And-Risk-Layer>: One composite envelope, rendered per gate, makes scope and reversibility evidence-backed instead of in-context judgment alone.
  (1) [Scope-At-Design]
  (2) [Risk-Before-Action]
  (3) [Impact-At-Completion]
  -----
  (4) The forward spine gains structured scope/risk surfacing without replacing its gates.

// --- Decision spine: passive capture that returns rationale to future work ---

[Passive-Capture]: Hooks capture operator decisions (MADR markdown) and agent observations (JSONL) automatically — no skill is modified and no one has to remember to log.
[Audit-Envelope-Capture]: The blast-radius audit hook appends the last status envelope to observations.jsonl on operator approval and Stop (Claude Code + Cursor), reusing the approval-phrase primitive.
[Records-Ride-With-Work]: At completion, the decision trail under docs/snowball/decisions/ is committed onto the same branch as the work it documents (preserve paths only).
[Distilled-To-Memory]: syncing-decisions-to-memory distills the logs into codebase-memory's project ADR, owning the TRADEOFFS and PHILOSOPHY sections.
[Future-Sessions-Recall]: recalling-project-context (plus a session-start ADR digest from disk) lets a later session recover TRADEOFFS/PHILOSOPHY and scoped MADRs before changing code.

<Decision-Spine>: A passive capture loop preserves why each choice was made and feeds it back to the next agent.
  (1) [Passive-Capture]
  (2) [Audit-Envelope-Capture]
  (3) [Records-Ride-With-Work]
  (4) [Distilled-To-Memory]
  (5) [Future-Sessions-Recall]
  -----
  (6) Rationale outlives the session that produced it and is recallable, in place, by whoever works the code next.

<Forward-Spine> +> [Trustworthy-Agent-Dev]
<Scope-And-Risk-Layer> +> [Trustworthy-Agent-Dev]
<Decision-Spine> +> [Trustworthy-Agent-Dev]

[Risk-Before-Action] +> [Evidence-Before-Claim]

// --- A tension the process deliberately holds ---

[Gate-Friction]: Hard gates add ceremony, which is pure overhead on a trivially simple task.
[Gate-Friction] - [Trustworthy-Agent-Dev]

[Scaled-Ceremony]: The gates scale to the work — a "design" can be a few sentences, worktrees fall back to the current dir, and argdown / chorus / blast-radius are opt-in or self-gating sub-skills reached only when the work warrants them.
[Scaled-Ceremony] - [Gate-Friction]
